NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE.

This is a research artifact. It measures two venue facts. It transmits no order,
sizes no position, and authorizes no capital.

The premium the measured route would harvest is payment for bearing crash risk.
VRPExperiment measured that payment at 198.111 bps of notional (n = 1,955) and
states plainly that it did not measure the liability: the tail absent from a
5.4-year sample is the entire risk a variance seller bears. The premium also
decays monotonically across that sample, 284.53 to 112.72 bps, a 60.4% fall.
